gle server instance:**\n\n| Scenario | Concurrent Users | Assumptions |\n|----------|-----------------|-------------|\n| **Conservative** | 50-100 | Build tier, active conversations |\n| **Moderate** | 500-1000 | Scale tier, mixed activity levels |\n| **Optimized** | 2000-5000 | Scale tier + optimizations below |\n\n## Optimization Recommendations\n\nTo support more users, you'd need to implement:\n\n1. **Request queuing and rate limiting** at the server level\n2. **Conversation history pruning** (keep last N messages)\n3. **Multiple server instances** with load balancing\n4. **API key rotation** across multiple Anthropic accounts\n5. **Caching** for repeated tool calls\n6. **Streaming responses** (the SDK supports it but server doesn't use it yet)\n\nThe server architecture is actually well-designed for horizontal scaling - you could run multiple instances behind a load balancer quite easily since each WebSocket session is independent.\n\n**Bottom line**: With default settings and a Scale tier API key, you could reasonably support **500-1000 concurrent active users** on a single server instance before hitting API rate limits.",
